Update an existing workflow version by its unique identifier.

USAGE:
  scw workflows version update <workflow-version-id ...> [arg=value ...]

ARGS:
  workflow-version-id   UUID of the workflow version to update
  [name]                Name of the workflow version
  [description]         Description of the workflow version
  [workflow-dsl]        DSL of workflow in YAML format based from https://open-workflow-specification.org/schemas/1.0.3/workflow.yaml
  [region=fr-par]       Region to target. If none is passed will use default region from the config (fr-par)

FLAGS:
  -h, --help                help for update
      --list-sub-commands   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta             Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string    The path to the config file
  -D, --debug            Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers       Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string    Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string   The config profile to use
